---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import ExampleRows from "../components/ExampleRows.astro";
import sample from "../data/sample-result.json";
---
<Page>
<Header isHome />
<main id="main">
<div id="landing">
<section class="band"><div class="hero wide enter">
  <h1>Check your repo before you hand it to an AI agent.</h1>
  <p class="hero-sub">13 file checks, the one thing to fix next, and the files that fix it. Your code never runs.</p>
  <form id="check-form" class="check" novalidate>
  <label for="repo-input">Paste a public GitHub repo</label>
  <div class="check-row">
    <input id="repo-input" name="url" type="text" inputmode="url" placeholder="https://github.com/owner/repo" autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false" autofocus />
    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary ctl">Check</button>
  </div>
  <div id="check-error" class="check-error" role="alert" hidden><p id="check-error-text" class="check-error-msg"></p></div>
  <div id="check-note" class="check-note"><span>Free, no account. 10 checks an hour.</span><a class="link ctl" href="#examples">No repo handy? See a real result</a></div>
  <noscript><p class="small muted">Running a check needs JavaScript. You can also run it on your machine: npx yokoten</p></noscript>
</form>
</div></section>
<section class="zone" id="examples"><div class="wide">
  <div class="results-head"><h2>Or open a real result</h2><span class="small muted">Last checked {sample.examplesCheckedOn}</span></div>
  <div class="results-grid">
    <div class="card results-group"><h3>Web2</h3><ExampleRows examples={sample.examples.filter((e) => e.group === "web2")} /></div>
    <div class="card results-group"><h3>Web3</h3><ExampleRows examples={sample.examples.filter((e) => e.group === "web3")} /></div>
  </div>
  <p class="results-note">Five checks need yokoten installed, so a repo without it tops out at 8 of 13. The file checks don't judge a repo's code.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="band" id="how"><div class="wide">
  <h2 class="home-title">It reads your repo. That's all.</h2>
  <ul class="facts">
    <li><strong>Your code never runs.</strong><p>No install, no build, no tests.</p></li>
    <li><strong>The network is cut.</strong><p>A throwaway sandbox, no connection.</p></li>
    <li><strong>Your repo doesn't change.</strong><p>We can't write to it. Nothing happens until you commit.</p></li>
  </ul>
  <p class="fine">Public repos only. It doesn't scan your code for vulnerabilities. Some files go to Muse Spark Open on Baseten to write the project section; Muse's text is cached for 24 hours.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="zone"><div class="wide more">
  <div class="card" id="terminal-card"><h3>Private repo? Prefer your terminal?</h3><p>Run the same check on your machine.</p><div class="card-action"><div class="cmd"><pre><code>npx yokoten</code></pre><button type="button" class="btn btn-line btn-sm ctl" data-copy="npx yokoten">Copy</button></div></div></div>
  <div class="card"><h3>Want this to stick?</h3><p>This page checks once. Installed, yokoten checks your agent's commands, your commits, and your pull requests.</p><div class="card-action"><a class="btn btn-line ctl" href="https://yokoten.app/">See what yokoten does</a></div></div>
</div></section>
</div>
<div id="app" hidden></div>
</main>
<Footer isHome />
<script src="../client/app.ts"></script>
</Page>
